cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  recalc: Trustworthiness assessments for summary statistics using
  recalculation checks
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hussey
    given-names: Ian
    email: ian.hussey@unibe.ch
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8906-7559"
abstract: >-
  Forensic meta-science tools that recalculate statistical results from the
  summary and test statistics reported in a paper. Reported numbers are rounded,
  and the analysis that produced them involves choices that are often left
  unstated, so a single reported result is compatible with a range of
  recalculated values rather than a single one. The package recomputes p-values
  and standardised effect sizes across the multiverse of defensible choices and
  returns the interval of recalculated values, together with whether the
  reported result falls inside it.
keywords:
  - meta-science
  - error detection
  - recalculation
  - effect sizes
  - R
